   \[
   3 \text{ ft} \times 100 \text{ cm/ft} + 6 \text{ in} \times 2.5 \text{ cm/in} = 900 \text{ cm} + 15 \text{ cm} = 915 \text{ cm}
   \]
   \[
   915 \text{ cm} \times \frac{1 \text{ m}}{100 \text{ cm}} = 9.15 \text{ m}
   \]

3. **Calculate the dose in milligrams:**
   \[
   17.5 \text{ mg/m}^2 \times (9.15 \text{ m})^2 = 17.5 \times 8.2625 = 296.3 \text{ mg}
   \]

Thus, the drug should be administered in a dose of \(\boxed{296.3 \text{ mg}}\) daily.

