- Concentration = 0.044% (w/v) = 0.044 g/100 mL  
- Volume = 10 mL  

First, we need to convert the concentration to g/mL:  
\[ \text{Concentration} = \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} = 0.000044 \text{ g/mL} \]  

Now, we can find the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL:  
\[ \text{Mass} = 0.000044 \text{ g/mL} \times 10 \text{ mL} = 0.00044 \text{ g} \]  

Finally, convert the mass from grams to milligrams:  
\[ \text{Mass} = 0.00044 \text{ g} \times \frac{1000 \text{ mg}}{1 \text{ g}} = 0.44 \text{ mg} \]  

Thus, there are \(\boxed{0.44 \text{ mg}}\) of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Phos-Flur Rinse.
