- Carbon is a reducing agent, and it reduces metal oxides by oxidizing itself to carbon dioxide.  
- The higher the reactivity of the metal, the harder it is to reduce its oxide.  
- Aluminum (Al) is highly reactive and its oxide (Al₂O₃) is highly stable.  
- PbO, ZnO, and Fe₂O₃ are less reactive than Al, and their oxides can be reduced by carbon.  

