","Supercritical fluid extraction (SFE) is a solvent extraction technique that uses supercritical fluids, such as carbon dioxide, to extract compounds from a solid or liquid matrix. It offers several advantages compared to other extraction methods, such as liquid extraction or steam distillation. Some of the advantages include:

