1. Let the cost price of the article be \( x \).  
2. The profit is 25%, so the total cost plus the profit is \( 1.25x \).  
3. The distance between the cost price and the after-detracted price is 10% of the load price.  
4. The after-detracted price is \( 0.9 \times \text{life price} = 0.9 \times 65.7 \).  
5. The equation is: \( 0.9 \times 65.7 = 1.25x \).  
6. Solving for \( x \):  
   \[
   x = \frac{0.9 \times 65.7}{1.25} = 50.00
   \]  
   The cost price of the article is \(\boxed{50.00}\).

</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

