   \int_{-1}^{2} \left(x^2 + 3 - 1\right) \, dx = \int_{-1}^{2} \left(x^2 + 2\right) \, dx
   \]

2. **Integrate the integrand:**
   \[
   \int_{-1}^{2} \left(x^2 + 2\right) \, dx = \frac{x^3}{3} + 2x \bigg]_{-1}^{2}
   \]

3. **Evaluate the integrand at the limits:**
   \[
   \left(\frac{2^3}{3} + 2 \cdot 2\right) - \left(\frac{(-1)^3}{3} + 2 \cdot (-1)\right) = \left(\frac{8}{3} + 4\right) - \left(-\frac{1}{3} - 2\right)
   \]

