Since the electron mass is negligible, the energy of the electron is given by \( E = \sqrt{m^2 c^4 + c^2 \mathbf{p}^2} \approx c|\mathbf{p}| \). Thus, \( E_i \approx c|\mathbf{p}_i) \) and \( E_f \approx c|\mathbf{p}_f) \). Substituting these into the expression for \( Q^2 \):
\[
Q^2 \approx (c|\mathbf{p}_f] - c|\mathbf{p}_i|)^2 - (\mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i)^2.
