\[
\sigma_{yr} = \frac{26 \times 10^9 \, \text{N m}^{-2} \times 0.286 \times 10^{-9} \, \text{m}}{6 \times 10^{-8} \, \text{m}} \left( \frac{1}{2} \frac{6 \times 10^{-8} \, \text{m}}{10^{-8} \, \text{m}} \right)^{1/2}
\]  
\[
\sigma_{yr} = 1.05 \times 10^6 \, \text{N m}^{-2}
\]  
\[
\sigma_{yr} = 1.05 \, \text{MPa}
\]  

Thus, the contribution of the hard particles to the tensile yield strength of the alloy is \(\boxed{1.05 \, \text{MPa}}\).
