\[
\Delta E \cdot \Delta t \geq \frac{h}{2\pi}
\]  
For the given lifetime (\(\Delta t = 2.0 \times 10^{-23}\) s), we can calculate the uncertainty in the energy:  
\[
\Delta E \geq \frac{h}{2\pi \Delta t} = \frac{6.626 \times 10^{-34} \text{ J s}}{2\pi \times 2.0 \times 10^{-23} \text{ s}} \approx 5.2 \times 10^{-12} \text{ J}
\]  
Convert this energy to MeV:  
\[
\Delta E \approx 5.2 \times 10^{-12} \text{ J} \times \frac{1 \text{ MeV}}{1.602 \times 10^{-13} \text{ J}} \approx 0.0052 \text{ MeV}
\]  
Thus, the typical range of outcomes of measurements of the \(\Sigma^+\) rest energy would be:  
\[
1385 \text{ MeV} \pm 0.0052 \text{ MeV}
\]  
