Air at 1 atm and 500°C flows over a plate 0.2 m long and 0.1 m wide with a Reynolds number of 40,000 (flow is along the 0.2 m side). The plate is maintained at 100°C, and the air temperature is 50°C.  
1. Determine the rate of heat transfer from the plate to the air.  
