   The work done per kg of air in an Otto cycle is:  
   \[
   w = \frac{544 \text{ kJ/kg}}{0.56} = 1000 \text{ kJ/kg}
   \]  
   Thus, the work done per kg of air is \(\boxed{1000 \text{ kJ/kg}}\).  

